  "interpretation": "CRITICAL: The two boards have INDEPENDENT microsecond clocks (esp_timer_get_time() counts from each board's own boot; they are NOT synchronised). Therefore we NEVER compute a difference between timestamps originating on different devices. Every reported statistic is a same-clock interval: TX-side (single device): submit->pulse and pulse->sendcb. RX-side (single device): edge->rxcb (headline one-way latency) and rxcb->accept. edge->rxcb captures radio TX + propagation + RX + callback delivery, all measured on the receiver's own clock. If a record has a zero timestamp for a field needed by an interval, that interval is skipped and counted under 'not_measurable' - we never substitute another timestamp or a host timestamp."
